        "geology": "Crystaline basement : the prevailing lithology is Precambrian migmatite,\r\nwhich has weathered to clayey saprolith.",
        "hydrology": "The area of investigation is characterized by 1100 mm precipitation with one rainy season from May to October which usually results in stream flow from August to November.",
        "soils": "The dominant soils in the catchment are \"sols ferrugineux tropicaux lessivés\" according to the French soil classification (Faure and Volkoff, Catena, 1998) and \"Lixisols\" according the World Reference Base (IUSS Working Group WRB, 2006).",
        "vegetation": "Vegetation is a patchwork of woodland, shrubland, crops (manioc, yam, maize, cotton and cashew nut are the most common crops) and herbaceous fallow."
      },
